  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Transportation obligated $85M in FY2027 to date. The agency recorded 479 awards with an average award size of $177K. Obligations fell 99.4% year over year relative to the prior fiscal year total. Fiscal-year history shows a step change before FY2027: FY22 totaled $8B, FY23 totaled $8.7B, FY24 totaled $8.6B, FY25 totaled $9B, and FY26 totaled $14.1B. The FY2027 to date portfolio concentrates in professional and IT services, with Engineering Services accounting for $39.9M and Computer Systems Design Services accounting for $21.9M. Software Publishers and Other Computer Related Services follow at $8.5M and $5.3M respectively. The vendor list is led by GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. at $19.3M, followed by RAYTHEON COMPANY at $11.9M and ARINC INCORPORATED at $10.6M. The FY2027 to date totals are partial, fiscal year to date, and reflect contract obligations rather than completed expenditures.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 spending compare to prior years?",
        "body": "The Department of Transportation obligated $85M in FY2027 to date, a sharp contraction from prior full-year totals. FY26 totaled $14.1B, FY25 totaled $9B, FY24 totaled $8.6B, FY23 totaled $8.7B, and FY22 totaled $8B. Obligations fell 99.4% year over year when comparing the FY2027 to date total with the prior period. The FY2027 figure is a fiscal year to date total and therefore partial."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which markets and vendors lead FY2027 obligations?",
        "body": "Engineering Services is the largest NAICS category at $39.9M, followed by Computer Systems Design Services at $21.9M and Software Publishers at $8.5M. Other notable categories include Other Computer Related Services at $5.3M and Facilities Support Services at $2.7M. GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. leads vendors with $19.3M, followed by RAYTHEON COMPANY at $11.9M and ARINC INCORPORATED at $10.6M. Several smaller vendors together account for the remaining FY2027 to date obligations."
      }
    ]
